## Auth & Proxy

- `proxy.ts` → cookie presence check → redirect to `/login`. Dashboard layout re-verifies JWT.
- Public: `/login`, `/api/*`, `/employee-booking`, legal pages, static assets.
- **Owner-only pages:** `/audit-log`, `/settings`, `/bookings/reconciliation`, `/intakes` (Booking/Cancellation Granot cases), `/ingestion/granot` (Automation + Lifecycle, including case/job detail). Exception: `/ingestion/granot/lifecycle/health` is Owner/Admin because the server health GET is Owner/Admin and Workflow Observational links here.
- Proxy flow: require admin session → validate relative path → `canProxyVantagePath(role, method, path)` → strip browser `x-api-secret`/`authorization`/`cookie` → set `x-vantage-admin-{user-id,email,role}` (+ optional HMAC via `VANTAGE_ADMIN_PROXY_SIGNING_SECRET`) → `server/vantage-api/client.ts` attaches `x-api-secret`.
- Non-owners: blocked from reconciliation, Granot automation, Granot lifecycle **pages** / candidates / Booking commands, Google Drive, reporting mutations (GET reporting OK), registry mutations (some read-preview POSTs OK), DELETE, observability deletes. Allowed: operational PATCH/POST, sheet-sync retry, incident status, observability report run, standard Granot lifecycle **GET** (cases/jobs/health, not candidates).
- Never expose `VANTAGE_API_SECRET` or signing secrets to client / `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`.

## Frontend Route Surface

**Operational:** `/` (`HomeOverview` — live home; not the planned Daily View), `/form-leads`, `/duplicate-form-leads`, `/call-leads`, `/duplicate-call-leads`, `/bookings`, `/bookings/new`, `/bookings/reconciliation` (owner), `/cancellations`, `/cancellations/new`, `/intakes` (owner Booking/Cancellation Granot cases), `/customers`, `/agents`, `/testimonials`

**Insight:** `/analytics`, `/reports/agent-sales`

**Ops:** `/observational` (`?tab=overview|events|incidents|reports|notifications|sheet-sync`), `/operations-registry` (`?tab=overview|agents|merchants|sources|granot-sources|ringcentral|cpl|changes`), `/ingestion` (Best Relocation), `/ingestion/granot` (owner), `/ingestion/granot/lifecycle` (owner technical queue), `/intakes` (owner Booking/Cancellation cases), `/ingestion/granot/lifecycle/health` (Owner/Admin read-only), `/ingestion/granot/lifecycle/cases/[caseId]`, `/ingestion/granot/lifecycle/jobs/[jobNo]`, `/reporting`, `/reporting/[id]`, `/reporting/destinations`, `/reporting/destinations/[id]`, `/reporting/runs/[id]`

**Support:** `/search`, `/exports`, `/audit-log` (owner), `/settings` (owner)

**Public:** `/employee-booking`, `/privacy-policy`, `/terms-and-conditions`

- Prefer extending `operational-resource-page` config before forking model pages.
- Scope controls live in `components/layout/scope-aware-header-controls.tsx`; coerce `combined` before detail fetches.
- Historical scope is read-only; hide mutations. No delete UI in any scope unless an explicit owner-only observability delete path already exists.

## Browser → Backend Clients (`lib/api/`)

All operational/admin data goes through `/api/proxy/...` except local audit + public employee-booking.

| Client | Backend prefix / role |
|--------|------------------------|
| `admin.ts` | Browse/detail/search/facets/testimonials/analytics/overview/observability/sheet-sync/exports + public v1 writes (leads/bookings/cancellations/customers, referral/leadless) |
| `audit.ts` | Local `/api/audit-log` |
| `operationsRegistry.ts` + `registry*.ts` | `/api/v1/admin/operations-registry/*`, catalog agents/merchants, source-companies/granularities, Granot CRM sources, CPL schedules/corrections, RingCentral inbound routes |
| `registryRequest.ts` | Shared registry JSON helper + `RegistryApiError` |
| `ingestion.ts` | `/api/v1/admin/ingestion/*` (Best Relocation) |
| `granotAutomation.ts` | `/api/v1/admin/granot-automation/*` (additive compatibility projection; apply checkboxes follow `available_for_apply`; receipts show lifecycle IDs / pending / bounded outcome only) |
| `granotLifecycle.ts` | `/api/v1/admin/granot-lifecycle/*` masked read DTOs plus Owner standard/Referral create, update, cancellation, and No Action POSTs; candidate browsing and commands are Owner-only; `operations/health` is a policy-free Owner/Admin GET |
| `registryGranotCrmSources.ts` | `/api/v1/admin/granot-crm-sources` list/detail/update/activation |
| `reporting.ts`, `reportingDestinations.ts` | `/api/v1/admin/reporting/*` |
| `googleDrive.ts` | `/api/v1/admin/google-drive/*` (owner) |
| `bookingLeadReconciliation.ts` | `/api/v1/admin/booking-lead-reconciliations/*` (owner) |
| `carriers.ts`, `cplRates.ts`, `catalog.ts` | Carriers + legacy settings CPL/catalog helpers |
| `employeeBooking.ts` | Local `/api/employee-booking/*` (not proxy) |

Use `lib/api/filters.ts` + `url-state.ts` for URL-synced filters; `lib/query/keys.ts` for cache keys/invalidation (`queryKeys.observability`, `queryKeys` registry/reporting/granot/reconciliation roots). Lifecycle command invalidation lives in `lib/query/granotLifecycle.ts`.

Granot Automation source checkboxes follow server `compatibility.available_for_apply`. Disabled rows stay visible. Best Relocation Forms/Inbounds stay unchecked until the operator opts in. New labels stay visible but unavailable until linked in Operations Registry (`?tab=granot-sources`). Server reviewed-family inventory stays on the main-server Operations Registry doc.

### Granot lifecycle reads and Booking/Release commands

- Owner-only pages live under `/ingestion/granot/lifecycle` (technical queue + `cases/[caseId]` + `jobs/[jobNo]`). Booking and cancellation case review for the Owner lives at `/intakes`. Choosing a waiting intake stays on `/intakes?case=` and does not jump to `/ingestion/granot/lifecycle/cases/:id`. The in-place case view is action-first: a "How to finish this booking/cancellation" card plus the official Owner command form (lead, binder, deposit, agents, merchant from the Operations Registry catalog) appear before Granot evidence. `BookingCommandForm` is numbered like the manual booking form (1 choose lead, 2 official catalog details, then review). Granot evidence, evidence history, and the job timeline stay as reference `<details>` (open only when commands are unavailable). `isAllowedIntakeReturn` allows `/intakes` plus safe `/intakes?...` query strings (no `://` or `//`); the technical case page may use that back-link. `/ingestion/granot` remains Automation. Nested layout tabs: Automation, Lifecycle, Intakes (jumps to `/intakes`), and Health. `/ingestion/granot/lifecycle/health` is Owner/Admin read-only (`queryKeys.granotLifecycle.health()`), linked from the lifecycle dashboard and Workflow Observational overview.
- Browser code always uses the signed `/api/proxy/api/v1/...` boundary. Standard lifecycle GETs (including `operations/health`) are Owner/Admin at the proxy; candidates and every command are Owner-only. Only the exact standard/Referral create, update, cancellation, and No Action paths forward `Idempotency-Key`; browser secrets and actor headers are stripped before trusted headers are minted.
- Server DTOs remain semantic authority for source scope, matching, candidate eligibility, masking, timeline ordering, and operations health. Admin components render those DTOs and never open operational Mongo or recompute due work, p95, rates, or alerts.
- `queryKeys.granotLifecycle` is isolated from Employee Booking reconciliation and Granot Automation. `invalidateGranotLifecycleCommandViews` is invoked after Confirm Granot Booking, Update Existing Booking, and No Action (success and `409` refetch). Health uses `queryKeys.granotLifecycle.health()` and is not part of that command invalidation set.
- Live Owner command UI: open standard and Referral Booking cases use `booking-owner-actions`; Referral create starts with blank official fields and never shows candidate/attach controls. Open `kind:"release"`, `mode:"release"` cases use `release-owner-actions` for Create Cancellation, full Update Existing Booking, and No Action. All surfaces require server capabilities and explicit review before submit.
- Polling (case detail 15s) may refresh evidence and timelines but must preserve component-owned confirm/update/cancellation/No Action draft state. Booking replacement initializes once from the live Booking projection (including active catalog IDs), while Cancellation starts blank; neither uses Granot evidence as official defaults. `409` refetch preserves unsent values and never auto-resubmits. Booking and Release discriminants, sequences, and timeline entries never collapse. Release command capability follows the server gate; discrepancies remain false.

## Ownership Boundaries

- **Admin owns:** login/sessions, admin audit DB, UI, route handlers, TanStack Query, frontend constants, signed proxy BFF, public employee-booking nonce.
- **Main server owns:** operational DBs, business rules, sheet sync, analytics, registry, ingestion, Granot automation, Granot lifecycle, reporting delivery, Google Drive connection, reconciliation, exports.
- Do not open `vantagemovers` / `vantagemovershistorical` from admin.
- Settings CPL/catalog managers are legacy/compatibility; durable source/CPL/agent/merchant edits live in Operations Registry.
- Mutations must invalidate the relevant query keys (lists, details, search, audit, analytics, registry, reporting) where data can change.

## Quality Practices

- Keep secrets/Mongo/auth in `server/` or route handlers — never in client components.
- Validate proxy paths stay under `VANTAGE_API_BASE_URL`; reject absolute/`://` targets.
- CLI Admin Previews do not inherit branch-only env. When the API host is a protected Preview, set Preview-only `VANTAGE_API_PROTECTION_BYPASS` to the **server** project's automation bypass (never this project's `VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET`) and pass both values with `vercel deploy --env`. Do not set the bypass on Production Admin.
- Audit mutating + CSV/export proxy requests without masking successful backend responses.
- Prefer small focused modules in the owning feature folder.
- After substantive changes: `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, and relevant tests.
